{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1238593-adversary-of-the-righteous-adeimantus-new-raksha-character","id":1238593,"title":"Adversary of the Righteous Adeimantus: New Raksha Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-25T08:39:01-07:00","id":1238593,"title":"Adversary of the Righteous Adeimantus: New Raksha Character","content":"So the new Adversary is out and its a Raksha! He's got 13 charms and something called Wyldcraft that is similar to Sorcery. One really interesting part of the write-up is apparently vulnerability to iron is only the most common Fair Folk weakness. In Adeimantus's case he's more vulnerable to people that have Linguistics 0 and can't read the words covering his skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T09:31:25-07:00","id":1238603,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/247451/Adversaries-of-the-Righteous-Adeimantus\" target=\"_blank\">A link</a> for those who want to check it out themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T09:44:38-07:00","id":1238608,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see some Raksha charms generally, though a lot of them are quite specific to him. They could probably be modified to fit Raksha with different themes without a ton of difficulty though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T09:45:43-07:00","id":1238609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1238593-adversary-of-the-righteous-adeimantus-new-raksha-character?p=1238608#post1238608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice to see some Raksha charms generally, though a lot of them are quite specific to him. They could probably be modified to fit Raksha with different themes without a ton of difficulty though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was thinking the same thing. Its good to get a write-up for a actual Essence 5 noble and get an idea of that charm level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T17:38:36-07:00","id":1238729,"title":"","content":"So, thoughts:<br /> The Kinda Valkyrie is great, probably will use in the next big battle that occurs in the north? But good anyways. We now have...2 quasi-ghost ghost collectors? Neat.<br /> The Auroch is intreasting--it takes a lot to make a wild bull scary to me. <br /> And the Raksha...I am suprised. ONe, my Raksha noble must be thinking small potatoes. Two, This Raksha Finally Lines Up With Mine (Mine runs a monastary trapped outside creation, but still, he's a false enlightment promising guru...) Three, kinda getting King in Yellow vibes? I like this sort of cursed art horror. I could see a whole chronicle around him. Oh, and he has kris, which is cool too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T19:50:13-07:00","id":1238759,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I am so glad that Raksha are scary again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T21:07:19-07:00","id":1238776,"title":"","content":"I really like Adeimantus, he has a lot of synergistic powers that feel strongly, for lack of better words, fae. The presentation of the character's deal is on point, and the infectious fantasy of the mythic city lost in the Wyld is the kind of element that provides material for a whole story. Details like the Immaculate Order making basically information war on his scheme in addition to violently rooting out adherents help situate it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-26-2018, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:13:42-07:00","id":1238835,"title":"","content":"Ravagers (the term used for people that had become enthralled by the Fair Folk and worked to spread their influence) and Wyld breakthroughs have always been elements of the Raksha that I thought were the most interesting, and sadly neglected; they would often be mentioned as things that existed, but hardly ever got actual examples. The fact that certain Aspect Book Shogunate chapters invoked them is part of why I like those sections so much.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see a sample character that is frickin' all about those things, as well as how the nature of the breakthrough is a subtle and insidious transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:56:11-07:00","id":1238895,"title":"","content":"I read Adeimantus and immediately started pondering if I should integrate him into my existing game or start working on a plot to use him as the primary antagonist for a new game. I love pretty much everything about this character and it marks the second thing that 3E has succeeded on that prior editions never could, make me care about the Fair Folk. (The first thing was the lunars playtest making me excited about Lunars)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T17:29:12-07:00","id":1239093,"title":"","content":"I said something more elaborate in the thread on fae weaknesses, but I find interesting implications in Adiemantus with regards to what separates the noble Raksha from the common cataphract or Lorelai, as well as implementation of what it means for one to adopt and express a personal mythos that is more grounded and accessible, while conversely becoming more versatile. It also gives me ideas for possible duelling narratives between Raksha that are a bit more invested than shaping combat was.<br /> <br /> I'm actually thinking of oath children; that more than just being a Raksha born to secure a magical oath, and otherwise indistinguishable, that one's existence might be marked specifically by the details of the oath, and the circumstances that led up to it.<br /> <br /> I'm picturing savants who observe patterns in the phenomenon of Raksha alliance and rivalry, the actions undertaken to promote it, and the manner in which they seal accord by creating a new being, and wondering if that might actually constitute their process of courtship and mating.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I'm seeing a Raksha in discourse with some Creation-born, commenting that while they can see the appeal of some human carnal pleasures, they find the idea of it creating children unbearably dull, and furthermore can't see the point if the child's whole existence is not an expression of all of the details of events leading up to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}